[Music]  it had all the comforts of home the  ukrainian flag the national anthem and  cossack dancers wearing embroidered  shirts but this celebration is 12 000  kilometers away from kiev in the small  brazilian town of prudentopolis  a feast to welcome 63 ukrainian refugees  we wanted to show them that they can  feel at home here prudentopolis is  brazil's little ukraine pastor vitalia  moved from ukraine to prudentopolis four  years ago only to discover that almost  every corner of his new home reminded  him of his old one from the architecture  to the bible in cyrillic and the  catholic mass held in his native tongue  three-quarters of the 53 000 people  living in prudentopolis still speak  ukrainian and maintain the traditions of  their ancestors who started migrating to  brazil as early as the 1800s  i remember my father in the 1940s taking  in a couple who had fled the second  world war and i said it was the hustle  now prudentopolis is preparing for the  new wave of ukrainians fleeing from the  russian invasion  they were brought over by global kingdom  a worldwide network of churches who  promote humanitarian causes  we started preparing to take in refugees  last year after seeing the shocking  images of people hanging onto a plane  trying to escape the taliban regime in  afghanistan we did the paperwork to  bring afghan families over but by the  time they were able to reach brazil the  russian invasion of ukraine had started  we moved rapidly to bring the ukrainian  refugees on board  eleven ukrainian families were taken to  guara puava a city just 80 kilometers  from prudentopolis they were housed in  separate apartments in the same building  olga martinchok fled with her husband  and children from her son family was  traveling to poland when they received a  message that brazil was taking in  refugees  we heard about brazilian carnivals and  we heard about beaches here we heard  about amazonia and  forests and that it is a green country  and  beautiful people  actually we didn't know much  27 of the 36 ukrainian refugees living  here in guarapuava are children and  they're already studying in brazilian  schools like this one  alga's son emmanuel is in the same  classroom as another young refugee  when the teacher has trouble  communicating with children she uses her  phone as a translator  olga has no immediate plans for the  future her house in herasan is now being  occupied by russian troops  back in prudentopolis brazilians and  ukrainians are praying for the war to  end before that manika yanaki of al  jazeera prudentopolis  [Music]

